IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nsw-nouns`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales), Part 2 Words and expressions: sections 6 to 12.
-- Each rule of reading is a function over a small typed description of what the rule operates on.
-- A judgment the Act leaves open (whether the context or subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires) is a plain input.

§ `Part 2 Words and expressions`

§§ `6 Definitions to be read in context`

-- src:48 | 6 Definitions to be read in context
-- src:49 | Definitions that occur in an Act or instrument apply to the construction of the Act or instrument except in so far as the context or subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires.
@ref s 6 (src:48-49)
GIVEN `the definition occurs in the Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context or subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6 the definition applies to the construction of the Act or instrument` MEANS
    IF `the definition occurs in the Act or instrument`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the context or subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `7 Cognate words`

-- src:51 | 7 Cognate words
-- src:52 | If an Act or instrument defines a word or expression, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of the word or expression have corresponding meanings.
@ref s 7 (src:51-52)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument defines the word or expression` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form is another part of speech or grammatical form of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 7 the form has the corresponding meaning` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Act or instrument defines the word or expression`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the form is another part of speech or grammatical form of it`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

§§ `8 Gender and number`

-- src:56 | (a) a word or expression that indicates one or more particular genders shall be taken to indicate every other gender,
@ref s 8(a) (src:56)
GIVEN `the word or expression indicates one or more particular genders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(a) the word or expression is taken to indicate every other gender` MEANS
    IF `the word or expression indicates one or more particular genders` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:57 | (b) a reference to a word or expression in the singular form includes a reference to the word or expression in the plural form,
-- src:58 | (c) a reference to a word or expression in the plural form includes a reference to the word or expression in the singular form,
@ref s 8(b) and (c) (src:57-58)
GIVEN `the form of the word referred to` IS A GrammaticalNumber
      `the form asked about` IS A GrammaticalNumber
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(b) and (c) the reference to a word in one number includes a reference to it in the other number` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the word referred to`
    WHEN SingularForm THEN
        CONSIDER `the form asked about`
        WHEN PluralForm THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN SingularForm THEN NOTHING
    WHEN PluralForm THEN
        CONSIDER `the form asked about`
        WHEN SingularForm THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN PluralForm THEN NOTHING

-- src:59 | (d) a reference to a person does not exclude a reference to a corporation merely because elsewhere in the Act or instrument there is particular reference to a corporation (in whatever terms expressed), and
@ref s 8(d) (src:59)
GIVEN `elsewhere in the Act or instrument there is particular reference to a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(d) the reference to a person excludes a corporation merely because of the particular reference elsewhere` MEANS
    IF `elsewhere in the Act or instrument there is particular reference to a corporation` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:60 | (e) a reference to a person does not exclude a reference to an individual merely because elsewhere in the Act or instrument there is particular reference to an individual (in whatever terms expressed).
@ref s 8(e) (src:60)
GIVEN `elsewhere in the Act or instrument there is particular reference to an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8(e) the reference to a person excludes an individual merely because of the particular reference elsewhere` MEANS
    IF `elsewhere in the Act or instrument there is particular reference to an individual` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `9 Meaning of may and shall`

-- The two words section 9 speaks of.
DECLARE ModalWord IS ONE OF
    TheWordMay
    TheWordShall
    AnotherModalWord

-- src:63 | (1) In any Act or instrument, the word "may", if used to confer a power, indicates that the power may be exercised or not, at discretion.
@ref s 9(1) (src:63)
GIVEN word IS A ModalWord
      `it is used to confer a power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(1) the word indicates that the power may be exercised or not, at discretion` MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN TheWordMay THEN JUST `it is used to confer a power`
    WHEN TheWordShall THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnotherModalWord THEN NOTHING

-- src:64 | (2) In any Act or instrument, the word "shall", if used to impose a duty, indicates that the duty must be performed.
@ref s 9(2) (src:64)
GIVEN word IS A ModalWord
      `it is used to impose a duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) the word indicates that the duty must be performed` MEANS
    CONSIDER word
    WHEN TheWordShall THEN JUST `it is used to impose a duty`
    WHEN TheWordMay THEN NOTHING
    WHEN AnotherModalWord THEN NOTHING

§§ `10 Construction of amending Acts and instruments`

-- src:66 | 10 Construction of amending Acts and instruments
-- src:67 | Words and expressions that occur in an Act or instrument that amends or repeals some other Act or instrument have the same meanings as they have in the other Act or instrument.
@ref s 10 (src:66-67)
GIVEN `the Act or instrument amends or repeals some other Act or instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 the words have the same meanings as in the other Act or instrument` MEANS
    IF `the Act or instrument amends or repeals some other Act or instrument` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `11 Words etc in instruments under an Act have same meanings as in the Act`

-- src:69 | 11 Words etc in instruments under an Act have same meanings as in the Act
-- src:70 | Words and expressions that occur in an instrument have the same meanings as they have in the Act, or in the relevant provisions of the Act, under which the instrument is made.
@ref s 11 (src:69-70)
GIVEN `the words occur in an instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the words occur in the Act, or in the relevant provisions of the Act, under which the instrument is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11 the words have in the instrument the same meanings as they have in the Act` MEANS
    IF `the words occur in an instrument` AND `the words occur in the Act, or in the relevant provisions of the Act, under which the instrument is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `12 References to New South Wales to be implied`

-- What a reference is to, for section 12(1).
DECLARE SubjectOfAReference IS ONE OF
    AnOfficerOfficeOrStatutoryBody
    ALocalityJurisdictionOrOtherMatterOrThing
    ThingNotNamedInSection12

-- src:74 | (a) a reference to an officer, office or statutory body is a reference to such an officer, office or statutory body in and for New South Wales, and
-- src:75 | (b) a reference to a locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing is a reference to such a locality, jurisdiction or other matter or thing in and of New South Wales.
@ref s 12(1) (src:74-75)
GIVEN subject IS A SubjectOfAReference
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(1) the reference is to the thing in New South Wales` MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN AnOfficerOfficeOrStatutoryBody THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ALocalityJurisdictionOrOtherMatterOrThing THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN ThingNotNamedInSection12 THEN NOTHING

-- src:76 | (2) In any Act or instrument, a reference to a body constituted by or under an Act or instrument need not include the words "New South Wales" or "of New South Wales" merely because those words form part of the body's name or title.
@ref s 12(2) (src:76)
GIVEN `the words "New South Wales" or "of New South Wales" form part of the body's name or title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 12(2) the reference to the body must include the words New South Wales or of New South Wales` MEANS
    IF `the words "New South Wales" or "of New South Wales" form part of the body's name or title` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Tests: sections 6 to 12`

-- s 6: the definition applies unless the context otherwise indicates; a definition that does not occur in the Act is outside the section
#ASSERT `s 6 the definition applies to the construction of the Act or instrument` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6 the definition applies to the construction of the Act or instrument` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6 the definition applies to the construction of the Act or instrument` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 7: the condition is that the Act or instrument defines the word
#ASSERT `s 7 the form has the corresponding meaning` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7 the form has the corresponding meaning` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7 the form has the corresponding meaning` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 8
#ASSERT `s 8(a) the word or expression is taken to indicate every other gender` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(a) the word or expression is taken to indicate every other gender` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(b) and (c) the reference to a word in one number includes a reference to it in the other number` SingularForm PluralForm EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(b) and (c) the reference to a word in one number includes a reference to it in the other number` PluralForm SingularForm EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 8(b) and (c) the reference to a word in one number includes a reference to it in the other number` SingularForm SingularForm EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(b) and (c) the reference to a word in one number includes a reference to it in the other number` PluralForm PluralForm EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(d) the reference to a person excludes a corporation merely because of the particular reference elsewhere` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(d) the reference to a person excludes a corporation merely because of the particular reference elsewhere` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(e) the reference to a person excludes an individual merely because of the particular reference elsewhere` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 8(e) the reference to a person excludes an individual merely because of the particular reference elsewhere` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 9
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the word indicates that the power may be exercised or not, at discretion` TheWordMay TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the word indicates that the power may be exercised or not, at discretion` TheWordMay FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the word indicates that the power may be exercised or not, at discretion` TheWordShall TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(1) the word indicates that the power may be exercised or not, at discretion` AnotherModalWord TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the word indicates that the duty must be performed` TheWordShall TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the word indicates that the duty must be performed` TheWordShall FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 9(2) the word indicates that the duty must be performed` TheWordMay TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 10 and 11
#ASSERT `s 10 the words have the same meanings as in the other Act or instrument` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 10 the words have the same meanings as in the other Act or instrument` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11 the words have in the instrument the same meanings as they have in the Act` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 11 the words have in the instrument the same meanings as they have in the Act` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 11 the words have in the instrument the same meanings as they have in the Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 12
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the reference is to the thing in New South Wales` AnOfficerOfficeOrStatutoryBody EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the reference is to the thing in New South Wales` ALocalityJurisdictionOrOtherMatterOrThing EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 12(1) the reference is to the thing in New South Wales` ThingNotNamedInSection12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the reference to the body must include the words New South Wales or of New South Wales` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 12(2) the reference to the body must include the words New South Wales or of New South Wales` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
